<SiteLayout title="Privacy" alternateUrl="/no/privacy/" description="Privacy information for HackShack Labs: hosting, external links, affiliate referrals and contacting Ploos AS."><h1>Privacy</h1><p>HackShack Labs is published by Ploos AS and served as a static website. We do not require an account to read articles. The site is hosted through GitHub Pages. GitHub and your network provider may process technical connection data. External links, including the voluntary Ko-fi support link, can take you to third-party sites with their own privacy practices.</p><p>Some clearly disclosed affiliate links may let a partner attribute a referral or purchase and may involve cookies or other tracking on the partner's website. We do not claim those third-party services are tracking-free. Consult their notices before proceeding.</p><p>We will update this notice if analytics, embedded third-party services or additional tracking are introduced. The publisher and responsible contact is Ploos AS; privacy questions can be sent privately to <a href="mailto:pgo@ploos.no">pgo@ploos.no</a>. Public corrections can be raised through the <a href="https://github.com/Ploos-AS/hackshack-labs/issues">project issue tracker</a>; do not post personal data publicly.</p></SiteLayout>